<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Copies Secure Web Sessions (SWS) application detection and URL/domain
    inclusion/exclusion settings from an existing SWS policy to another policy.

.DESCRIPTION
    PowerShell 5.1-compatible test utility.

    This script does NOT change the CyberArk Identity application definition.
    It works only with the SWS public API and intentionally copies only the
    application-detection and URL/domain matching or exclusion configuration.

    The source policy is located by Identity application key. The target policy
    can be located by its Identity application key or application/policy name.

    To reduce dependency on hard-coded Edge API paths and request-body fields,
    the script downloads or reads CyberArk's official SWS Postman collection and
    discovers the following requests from the collection:
      - GET SWS policies
      - GET policy by ID
      - PUT policy application configuration

    Default behavior is REPORT ONLY. Use -Execute to send the PUT request.

    When no SWS token or token-helper parameters are supplied, the script prompts
    immediately for an authentication method. The regular Identity user login is
    not reused because the SWS public API requires an SWS service account.

.EXAMPLE
    .\Test-Clone-SwsApplicationConfiguration.ps1 `
        -TargetApplicationName 'svc-gcp-app-001' `
        -SwsTenantId '<SWS tenant ID>' `
        -TokenHelperJarPath 'C:\Tools\public-api-auth-helper-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT-application.jar' `
        -SwsServiceAccountSecretPath 'C:\Secure\sws-service-account.json'

    Builds and exports the proposed payload but does not update SWS.

.EXAMPLE
    .\Test-Clone-SwsApplicationConfiguration.ps1 `
        -TargetApplicationName 'svc-gcp-app-001' `
        -SwsTenantId '<SWS tenant ID>' `
        -TokenHelperJarPath 'C:\Tools\public-api-auth-helper-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT-application.jar' `
        -SwsServiceAccountSecretPath 'C:\Secure\sws-service-account.json' `
        -Execute

    Copies the SWS detection and URL exemption settings and then verifies them.

.NOTES
    Source Identity app key default:
    3c696971-5812-430a-88b1-417c6be2628f

    The SWS v2-edge API is subject to change. This script therefore derives the
    request URLs and payload shape from the current official Postman collection.
#>

[CmdletBinding()]
